#
# Declarative structural assertions for the mathematics slice — the slice-resident
# test-DSL twin of the asserted-TBox MUST / MUST-NOT invariants. Each assertion runs
# as a SPARQL ASK over the mathematics module graph (gmeow:scopeModule) under the
# native Rust slicetest harness (crates/slicetest).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/> .

# --- 1. The number-system containment tower ℕ ⊑ ℤ ⊑ ℚ ⊑ ℝ ⊑ ℂ (MUST) ---
ex:saNumberTower a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:NaturalNumber  rdfs:subClassOf math:Integer .
    math:Integer        rdfs:subClassOf math:RationalNumber .
    math:RationalNumber rdfs:subClassOf math:RealNumber .
    math:RealNumber     rdfs:subClassOf math:ComplexNumber .
    math:ComplexNumber  rdfs:subClassOf math:Number .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The five nested number systems MUST form the containment tower ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ as rdfs:subClassOf edges, so a value in an inner system is entailed to be a value of every outer one." .

# --- 2. Every bedrock failure class subclasses math:MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:UnsituatedNumber          rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ExactApproximateConflation rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ConstantAsDecimalLiteral  rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:StringOnlyMemberCondition rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnqualifiedComplement     rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:AmbiguousSetExtent        rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnframedFunction          rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each of the seven bedrock hard-rule failures MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 2b. The flagship-manifest failure class subclasses math:MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saFlagshipFailureTyped a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:UnwiredFlagshipScenario rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The unwired-flagship failure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so an unwired acceptance scenario is a typed, queryable violation like every other math: hard-rule failure." .

# --- 2c. The five flagship scenarios are present and fully wired (MUST) ---
ex:saFlagshipCoverage a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModuleAndExamples ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX exa: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/acceptance/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?scenario {
        exa:e8Symmetry exa:homomorphicEncryption exa:proofAsProcess
        exa:rBridge exa:aiSelfStructure
    }
    ?scenario a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ;
        gmeow:demonstratedByExample ?ex ;
        gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency ?cq ;
        gmeow:demonstratedByProducer ?prod ;
        gmeow:guardedByCounterExample ?ce ;
        gmeow:enforcesFailureClass ?fc .
    ?fc rdfs:subClassOf+ math:MathConformanceFailure .
    FILTER(isLiteral(?ex) && isIRI(?cq) && isLiteral(?prod) && isLiteral(?ce) && isIRI(?fc))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "This layer's five flagship acceptance scenarios MUST each be present as a gmeow:FlagshipScenario binding its worked example, competency question, native producer, counter-example, and a real math:MathConformanceFailure subclass. If any of the five is absent or missing a link, the acceptance bar is not met and this assertion fails — the depth bar is a contract, not prose." .

# --- 3. The seven arithmetic operators exist as math:ArithmeticOperation (MUST) ---
ex:saArithmeticOperators a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
ASK {
    math:Addition       a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Subtraction    a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Multiplication a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Division       a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Exponentiation a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Root           a math:ArithmeticOperation .
    math:Logarithm      a math:ArithmeticOperation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Addition, multiplication, exponentiation, and their inverses MUST exist as math:ArithmeticOperation individuals." .

# --- 4. No math: property asserts an EL-forbidden OWL characteristic (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saNoForbiddenCharacteristics a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    ?p a ?characteristic .
    FILTER (?characteristic IN (
        owl:SymmetricProperty, owl:AsymmetricProperty, owl:IrreflexiveProperty,
        owl:FunctionalProperty, owl:InverseFunctionalProperty
    ))
    FILTER (STRSTARTS(STR(?p), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "No math: property MUST carry a symmetric, asymmetric, irreflexive, functional, or inverse-functional OWL characteristic — the profile is kept EL-clean; such characteristics (e.g. the symmetry of math:inverseFunction) are documented in prose. Transitivity (math:subsetOf, math:subsystemOf) is EL-valid and permitted." .

# --- 5. Order-bearing composition refines math:functionComposition (MUST) ---
ex:saCompositionOrder a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:compositionOuter rdfs:subPropertyOf math:functionComposition .
    math:compositionInner rdfs:subPropertyOf math:functionComposition .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Function composition is non-commutative (g ∘ f ≠ f ∘ g), so the composite→component relation MUST carry order: math:compositionOuter (applied second) and math:compositionInner (applied first) refine math:functionComposition. A single order-agnostic property would lose which component is inner and which is outer." .

# --- 6. The group subsumption tower Magma ⊒ … ⊒ AbelianGroup (MUST) ---
ex:saGroupTower a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:Magma        rdfs:subClassOf math:AlgebraicStructure .
    math:Semigroup    rdfs:subClassOf math:Magma .
    math:Monoid       rdfs:subClassOf math:Semigroup .
    math:Group        rdfs:subClassOf math:Monoid .
    math:AbelianGroup rdfs:subClassOf math:Group .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The algebraic hierarchy MUST be subsumption: an AbelianGroup is a Group is a Monoid is a Semigroup is a Magma is an AlgebraicStructure, each an rdfs:subClassOf edge, so an instance of a lower structure is entailed to be an instance of every weaker one." .

# --- 7. The ring/module towers Field ⊑ … ⊑ Ring and VectorSpace ⊑ Module (MUST) ---
ex:saRingModuleTower a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:Ring            rdfs:subClassOf math:AlgebraicStructure .
    math:CommutativeRing rdfs:subClassOf math:Ring .
    math:Field           rdfs:subClassOf math:CommutativeRing .
    math:PolynomialRing  rdfs:subClassOf math:CommutativeRing .
    math:Module          rdfs:subClassOf math:AlgebraicStructure .
    math:VectorSpace     rdfs:subClassOf math:Module .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The ring and module towers MUST be subsumption: a Field is a CommutativeRing is a Ring, a PolynomialRing is a CommutativeRing, and a VectorSpace is a Module — so a field is entailed to be a ring and every ring-level axiom applies." .

# --- 8. A morphism is NOT a function (avoids the set-typed framing gate) (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saMorphismNotFunction a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:Morphism rdfs:subClassOf math:Function .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:Morphism MUST NOT be a subclass of math:Function: a morphism's domain and codomain range over algebraic structures, not bare sets, so making it a function would let the set-typed math:FunctionFramingShape misfire on structure-typed domains. Morphism is its own object-layer parent." .

# --- 9. The algebra failure classes subclass math:MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saAlgebraFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:IncompleteAlgebraicStructure rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The algebra hard-rule failure math:IncompleteAlgebraicStructure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 10. The homomorphism hierarchy, incl. AutomorphismGroup ⊑ Group (MUST) ---
ex:saHomomorphismHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:Homomorphism      rdfs:subClassOf math:Morphism .
    math:GroupHomomorphism rdfs:subClassOf math:Homomorphism .
    math:RingHomomorphism  rdfs:subClassOf math:Homomorphism .
    math:Isomorphism       rdfs:subClassOf math:Homomorphism .
    math:Automorphism      rdfs:subClassOf math:Isomorphism .
    math:AutomorphismGroup rdfs:subClassOf math:Group .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The structure-preserving maps MUST form the declared hierarchy, and crucially math:AutomorphismGroup MUST be a subclass of math:Group: a symmetry group IS an automorphism group, the identity that lets E8's Weyl action, det, and a homomorphic-encryption scheme be the same kind of object." .

# --- 11. The homomorphism failure classes subclass MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saHomomorphismFailures a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:UnderspecifiedHomomorphism rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:StringOnlyPreservationLaw  rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Both homomorphism hard-rule failures MUST be subclasses of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 12. The Weyl group IS an automorphism group IS a group (MUST) ---
ex:saWeylGroupIsSymmetry a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:WeylGroup rdfs:subClassOf math:AutomorphismGroup .
    math:AutomorphismGroup rdfs:subClassOf math:Group .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A root system's symmetry group is its Weyl group, which MUST be a math:AutomorphismGroup and hence a math:Group — the identity that makes E8's symmetry expressible with the same machinery as det and homomorphic encryption." .

# --- 12b. The unification failure classes subclass MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saUnificationFailures a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:UnanchoredAutomorphismGroup rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:WrongE8WeylOrder            rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:automorphismGroupOf         a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The two unification hard-rule failures MUST be typed math:MathConformanceFailure, and math:automorphismGroupOf MUST exist: every math:AutomorphismGroup is the symmetry of some structure (anchored through math:automorphismGroupOf), and a root system claiming to be E8 with a wrong Weyl order is rejected by value — so a violation of either is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 12d. A ring's distributivity gate is a typed failure + refined property (MUST) ---
ex:saRingDistributivity a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:NonDistributiveRing      rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:satisfiesDistributivity  rdfs:subPropertyOf math:satisfiesAxiom .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The distributivity hard-rule failure math:NonDistributiveRing MUST be a typed math:MathConformanceFailure, and math:satisfiesDistributivity MUST refine math:satisfiesAxiom — a ring must name a distributivity law specifically, and that law is still one of the axioms the general structure gate sees." .

# --- 13. IncompleteLieStructure subclasses MathConformanceFailure (MUST) ---
ex:saLieFailure a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:IncompleteLieStructure rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The Lie hard-rule failure math:IncompleteLieStructure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 14. Homomorphic encryption IS a ring homomorphism (the bridge) (MUST) ---
ex:saHeIsRingHomomorphism a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme rdfs:subClassOf math:EncryptionScheme .
    math:HomomorphicEncryptionScheme rdfs:subClassOf math:RingHomomorphism .
    math:homomorphicOver rdfs:subPropertyOf math:preservedOperation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A homomorphic-encryption scheme MUST be both a math:EncryptionScheme and a math:RingHomomorphism, and math:homomorphicOver MUST refine math:preservedOperation — so HE is the same map+law object as det and the Weyl action, and its homomorphic property is a preserved operation." .

# --- 15. The lattice-hardness assumptions and HE failure exist (MUST) ---
ex:saHeVocabulary a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:learningWithErrors     a math:LatticeHardnessAssumption .
    math:ringLearningWithErrors a math:LatticeHardnessAssumption .
    math:UnderspecifiedEncryptionScheme rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The LWE and RLWE hardness assumptions MUST exist as math:LatticeHardnessAssumption individuals, and the HE hard-rule failure MUST be a typed math:MathConformanceFailure." .

# --- 16. Algebra dogfoods GMEOW via the one-way math:formalizes bridge (MUST) ---
ex:saDogfoodFormalizes a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    math:Lattice math:formalizes gmeow:tuningSystemJustIntonation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Algebra MUST ground at least one GMEOW domain concept through the one-way math:formalizes annotation (Principle 19): a prime-limit just-intonation tuning is a free abelian lattice, so math:Lattice formalizes gmeow:tuningSystemJustIntonation — surfaced in the domain term's documentation with the domain slice asserting no math: triple. This makes algebra grounding for the ontology, not a math island." .

# --- 17. The measure subclasses specialize math:Measure (MUST) ---
ex:saMeasureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:LebesgueMeasure    rdfs:subClassOf math:Measure .
    math:CountingMeasure    rdfs:subClassOf math:Measure .
    math:ProbabilityMeasure rdfs:subClassOf math:Measure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The Lebesgue, counting, and probability measures MUST specialize math:Measure, so the probability bridge (a probability measure is a measure of total mass one) and the continuous/discrete cases are entailed rather than re-minted." .

# --- 18. The seven SI base dimensions exist as math:BaseDimension (MUST) ---
ex:saBaseDimensions a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
ASK {
    math:lengthDimension            a math:BaseDimension .
    math:massDimension              a math:BaseDimension .
    math:timeDimension              a math:BaseDimension .
    math:electricCurrentDimension   a math:BaseDimension .
    math:temperatureDimension       a math:BaseDimension .
    math:amountOfSubstanceDimension a math:BaseDimension .
    math:luminousIntensityDimension a math:BaseDimension .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The seven SI base dimensions (length, mass, time, electric current, thermodynamic temperature, amount of substance, luminous intensity) MUST exist as math:BaseDimension individuals — the generators of the ℚ-vector space of dimensions." .

# --- 19. The measure-and-dimension failure classes subclass the parent (MUST) ---
ex:saMeasureDimensionFailures a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:IncompleteMeasure               rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ProbabilityMeasureMassViolation rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:IncompleteIntegral              rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UndimensionedQuantity           rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:MalformedDimension              rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:DimensionalInhomogeneity        rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each measure-and-dimension hard-rule failure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation — including the reasoned math:DimensionalInhomogeneity — is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- Analysis & geometry subsumption invariants (ANALYSIS-AND-GEOMETRY) ----- #

ex:saAnalysisGeometryTower a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:HomologyGroup       rdfs:subClassOf math:AbelianGroup .
    math:MetricTensor        rdfs:subClassOf math:TensorField .
    math:ContinuousMap       rdfs:subClassOf math:Morphism .
    math:Homeomorphism       rdfs:subClassOf math:ContinuousMap .
    math:LorentzianManifold  rdfs:subClassOf math:SmoothManifold .
    math:SmoothManifold      rdfs:subClassOf math:Manifold .
    math:Manifold            rdfs:subClassOf math:TopologicalSpace .
    math:Integral            rdfs:subClassOf math:BindingExpression .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The analysis-and-geometry hierarchy MUST hold as asserted rdfs:subClassOf edges: a homology group is an abelian group (so it inherits the algebra frame), a metric tensor is a tensor field, a continuous map is a morphism and a homeomorphism is a continuous map, the manifold tower Lorentzian ⊑ smooth ⊑ manifold ⊑ topological space, and the integral is a binding expression (∫ is a binder like d/dx, ∑, lim)." .

ex:saAnalysisGeometryFailures a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:MalformedArgumentSlot           rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:MalformedBindingExpression      rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UndeclaredLogicLowering         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnscopedVariableOccurrence      rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedDerivative        rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedLimit             rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedConvergence       rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UndeclaredTopologicalProperty   rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedManifold          rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedChart             rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:DimensionMismatch               rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each analysis-and-geometry hard-rule failure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a violation — a malformed argument slot or binder, a silent logic: lowering, an unscoped occurrence, an underspecified derivative/limit/convergence/manifold/chart, an assumed topological property, or a dimension mismatch — is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- 20. Every topological property's math:definingLaw resolves to a law or boundary (MUST) ---
ex:saTopologicalLawBacking a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?concept math:definingLaw ?law .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?law a logic:Formula }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?law logic:expressivenessBoundary ?boundary }
  }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Every concept carrying math:definingLaw MUST resolve to a real first-order logic:Formula (math:continuityLaw, math:connectednessLaw, math:t0SeparationLaw … math:normalitySeparationLaw) or a recorded logic:expressivenessBoundary boundary (math:compactnessBoundary) — turning 'backed by a law' from prose into an open, machine-checked, type-checked invariant. The ASK is OPEN (it hand-enumerates no concept: it finds NO math:definingLaw edge whose target is neither a logic:Formula NOR carries logic:expressivenessBoundary) and TYPE-CHECKED (a dangling or mistyped backing edge — one pointing at a bare type — fails it). A new grounded property joins the audit simply by carrying math:definingLaw, with no list to maintain." .

# --- Linear algebra & learning: subsumption and framing invariants (MUST) --- #
ex:saLinearAlgebraSubsumption a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:InnerProductSpace       rdfs:subClassOf math:VectorSpace .
    math:Subspace                rdfs:subClassOf math:VectorSpace .
    math:LatentSpace             rdfs:subClassOf math:VectorSpace .
    math:ParameterSpace          rdfs:subClassOf math:VectorSpace .
    math:OrthogonalComplement    rdfs:subClassOf math:Complement .
    math:LinearMap               rdfs:subClassOf math:Function .
    math:CovarianceOperator      rdfs:subClassOf math:LinearMap .
    math:Embedding               rdfs:subClassOf math:Function .
    math:KnowledgeGraphEmbedding rdfs:subClassOf math:Embedding .
    math:PCAAnalysis             rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Activity .
    math:ResidualInterpretationClaim rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Observation .
    math:AttentionOperation      rdfs:subClassOf math:Operation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The linear-algebra-and-learning terms MUST sit in their proper places in the object hierarchy: the space classes under math:VectorSpace, the orthogonal complement under math:Complement (so it inherits the complement contract), linear/covariance/embedding maps under math:Function, a PCA under gmeow:Activity (a process) and a residual interpretation under gmeow:Observation (a vantage-held claim), and the attention operator under math:Operation (so it applies inside the reused expression AST)." .

# --- Every linear-algebra-and-learning failure is typed (MUST) -------------- #
ex:saLinearAlgebraFailures a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:IncompletePCAAnalysis           rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ResidualMeaningAsProperty       rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnderspecifiedEmbedding         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:MalformedTensorComputationGraph rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnframedWeightTensor            rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ApplicationOperatorCardinality  rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each linear-algebra-and-learning hard-rule failure MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so an unqualified orthogonal complement, an incomplete PCA, a residual meaning stamped as a property, an underspecified embedding, a malformed tensor graph, an unframed weight tensor, or an application applying other than exactly one operator is a typed, queryable object." .

# --- Meaning is representable only as a vantage-held claim (MUST-NOT) -------- #
ex:saNoDirectResidualMeaningProperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    ?p a ?ptype .
    FILTER(?ptype IN (owl:DatatypeProperty, owl:ObjectProperty, rdf:Property))
    FILTER(?p IN (math:residualMeaning, math:latentDimensionMeaning, math:componentMeaning, math:meaning))
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The slice MUST NOT mint a direct residual/latent/component 'meaning' property — whether minted as a datatype, object, or plain RDF property: semantic meaning read off geometry is a vantage-held math:ResidualInterpretationClaim (a gmeow:Observation), never an intrinsic property of the vector, so the property-form of meaning is unauthorable by construction." .

# --- The expression-rendering seam grafts onto lang:Rendering (MUST) -------- #
ex:saExpressionRenderingGraftsLang a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:ExpressionRendering a owl:Class ;
        rdfs:subClassOf lang:Rendering .
    math:rendersAs a owl:ObjectProperty .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The math slice MUST re-base its rendering seam onto the general lang:Rendering theory rather than forking it: math:ExpressionRendering MUST be an owl:Class that subclasses lang:Rendering, and the convenience shortcut math:rendersAs MUST exist as an owl:ObjectProperty, so a rendered mathematical expression reads its content, convention, and preservation off the shared lang: rendering facets." .

# --- A well-formed ExpressionRendering carries content, convention, preservation (MUST) --- #
ex:saExpressionRenderingFacets a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModuleAndExamples ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    ?r a math:ExpressionRendering ;
        lang:renderedContent ?content ;
        lang:renderingKind lang:renderingNotation ;
        lang:renderingConvention ?convention ;
        lang:renderingPreservation logic:ExactPreservation .
    ?content a math:ApplicationExpression .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "An authored math:ExpressionRendering MUST name the mathematical expression it renders through lang:renderedContent, fix its kind to lang:renderingNotation, name the notation convention through lang:renderingConvention, and carry a logic:PreservationKind judgment through lang:renderingPreservation — the exact inputs a MathML or LaTeX projection target reads off the record — so the rendering seam is a fully specified crossing rather than a bare display string." .

# --- Bridge runs are activities; the three bridges subclass the unifier (MUST) --- #
ex:saIngestRunActivityHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:IngestRun     rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Activity .
    math:RIngestRun    rdfs:subClassOf math:IngestRun .
    math:ONNXIngestRun rdfs:subClassOf math:IngestRun .
    math:ProofIngestRun rdfs:subClassOf math:IngestRun .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A bridge run is the executed put-leg occurrence of a lift — a process — so math:IngestRun MUST be a gmeow:Activity, and the three concrete bridges (R, ONNX, proof) MUST subclass the shared unifier, carrying the shared bridge contract once on the abstract run." .

# --- The QED result is a result object, NOT an observation (MUST) ----------- #
ex:saVerificationResultIsObject a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:FormalVerificationResult rdfs:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:FormalVerificationResult is the structured RESULT OBJECT of checking a proof, so it MUST be a math:MathematicalObject — distinct from the process (the run) and the held claim (the observation)." .

# --- The QED result MUST NOT be typed an observation (MUST-NOT) ------------- #
ex:saVerificationResultNotObservation a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:FormalVerificationResult rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Observation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:FormalVerificationResult MUST NOT be a gmeow:Observation: typing the result object as the held claim is the math:ResultRoleConflation — the verdict is HELD BY a separate observation with the checker as vantage, never IS-A one." .

# --- The QED result object is disjoint from the observation (MUST) ---------- #
ex:saVerificationResultDisjointObservation a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:FormalVerificationResult owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The result object of the process / result / claim separation is never the held claim, so math:FormalVerificationResult MUST be owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation — the OWL-axiom gate backing math:ResultRoleConflation. The native DL coherence gate reads the disjointness directly, forcing any individual typed both a verification result and an observation to owl:Nothing, mirroring lang:InterpretationAct owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation." .

# --- The bridge failure classes are typed conformance failures (MUST) ------- #
ex:saBridgeFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:UnliftableIngest             rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UngroundedIngestRun          rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UngroundedVerificationResult rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnfittedModel                rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ResultRoleConflation         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Every bridge failure is a typed, queryable object, so each MUST subclass math:MathConformanceFailure — a violation is a first-class failure class, not a log line." .

# --- An inference/analysis process is never an observation (MUST) ----------- #
ex:saProcessNotObservation a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:IngestRun   owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation .
    math:PCAAnalysis owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "An inference or analysis process is a gmeow:Activity, never the claim about its results, so the math process classes MUST be owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation — the OWL-axiom gate backing math:ProcessObservationConflation, mirroring lang:InterpretationAct owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation." .

# --- The process/result/claim separation failures are typed (MUST) ---------- #
ex:saSeparationFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:ProcessObservationConflation rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UngroundedResultClaim        rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:ResultRoleConflation         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The process / result / claim separation names three typed failures — conflating the process with the claim (math:ProcessObservationConflation), leaving a result claim ungrounded by a vantage (math:UngroundedResultClaim), and roling the result object as the claim (math:ResultRoleConflation) — so each MUST subclass math:MathConformanceFailure as a first-class, queryable object." .

# --- Probability: the event-set is disjoint from the occurrent (MUST) -------- #
ex:saProbabilityEventDisjointOccurrent a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:ProbabilityEvent owl:disjointWith logic:Event .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:ProbabilityEvent is the measure-theoretic sense — a measurable SET OF OUTCOMES — whereas a logic:Event is an occurrent (something that happens in time), so the two MUST be held owl:disjointWith: a rain occurrence and the rain event-set in a forecast space are never conflated. The OWL-axiom gate backing math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentConflation, whose paired SHACL (Rule P11) surfaces the same conflation as a finding." .

# --- Probability: a probability value is disjoint from odds and log-odds (MUST) --- #
ex:saProbabilityValueDisjointScales a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:OddsValue    owl:disjointWith math:ProbabilityValue .
    math:LogOddsValue owl:disjointWith math:ProbabilityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:ProbabilityValue is ALWAYS in the closed unit interval [0, 1]; math:OddsValue (0, ∞) and math:LogOddsValue (−∞, ∞) are lawful probability-SCALE transforms, NOT probabilities, so each MUST be held owl:disjointWith math:ProbabilityValue — a consumer seeing a math:ProbabilityValue may correctly assume [0, 1], and handing it an odds/log-odds is the caught math:ProbabilityScaleConflation (paired SHACL Rule P2), never a silent one." .

# --- Probability: every probability + projection failure is typed (MUST) ----- #
ex:saProbabilityFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
        VALUES ?fc {
            math:ProbabilityOutOfBounds
            math:ProbabilityScaleConflation
            math:ProbabilityEventOccurrentConflation
            math:UnframedProbabilityValue
            math:ConfidenceAsProbability
            math:IncompleteProbabilitySpace
            math:UnscopedRandomVariable
            math:MissingDistributionParameterization
            math:DistributionParameterRoleCardinality
            math:DistributionParameterConstraint
            math:UnconditionedAssertion
            math:MissingProbabilityModelLowering
            math:IncompleteDependencyModel
            math:ExactPreservationViolated
            math:ProjectionConfidenceAsProbability
            math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization
        }
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?fc rdfs:subClassOf+ math:MathConformanceFailure . }
    }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each of the sixteen probability-layer and projection-side hard-rule failures MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so every violation — an out-of-bounds probability, a conflated scale, an event/occurrent conflation, an unframed value, a confidence read as probability, an incomplete space, an unscoped random variable, a missing/miscardinalitied/mis-constrained parameterization, an unconditioned assertion, a missing lowering, an incomplete dependency model, an exactness overclaim, or a silent confidence/parameterization drop at the projection seam — is a typed, queryable object. The ASK is a for-all over a VALUES list (it finds NO enumerated failure that fails to subclass the parent), so a new probability failure joins the audit by being added to the list." .

# --- Probability: an MCMC run is a process (an Activity), not a claim (MUST) -- #
ex:saMcmcRunIsActivity a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:MCMCRun rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Activity .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A math:MCMCRun is the sampling PROCESS that draws a math:PosteriorSample from a posterior — an occurrent, distinct from its result sample and from any claim about the posterior — so it MUST be a subclass of gmeow:Activity, carrying the process/result/claim separation of the observations spine and letting 'which run produced these draws and diagnostics' be answered through gmeow:wasGeneratedBy." .

# --- Inference: a frequentist result is disjoint from a Bayesian result (MUST) --- #
ex:saFrequentistBayesianDisjoint a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK {
    math:FrequentistResult owl:disjointWith math:BayesianResult .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The two inference-paradigm result families are first-class and neither is privileged, but a single result is NEVER both — a p-value is not a posterior probability, a confidence interval is not a credible interval — so math:FrequentistResult MUST be held owl:disjointWith math:BayesianResult. The paradigm axis is a PARTIAL classification (only paradigm-exclusive kinds are placed under the two families, a paradigm-neutral math:Estimate or math:Residual under neither), and this disjointness is the OWL-axiom gate the native DL coherence check reads to force any individual typed both a frequentist and a Bayesian result to owl:Nothing." .

# --- Inference: the interval kinds inherit paradigm; CI ⊥ Credible is ENTAILED (MUST) --- #
ex:saIntervalParadigmPlacement a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:ConfidenceInterval rdfs:subClassOf math:FrequentistResult .
    math:ConfidenceRegion   rdfs:subClassOf math:FrequentistResult .
    math:CredibleInterval   rdfs:subClassOf math:BayesianResult .
    math:CredibleRegion     rdfs:subClassOf math:BayesianResult .
    math:BayesFactor        rdfs:subClassOf math:BayesianResult .
    math:PosteriorProbability rdfs:subClassOf math:BayesianResult .
    math:PredictionInterval rdfs:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
    math:ToleranceInterval  rdfs:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
    math:EffectSize         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
    math:Prediction         rdfs:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The paradigm-exclusive interval, region, and evidence kinds MUST inherit their family: math:ConfidenceInterval and math:ConfidenceRegion under math:FrequentistResult (coverage under a sampling procedure), math:CredibleInterval, math:CredibleRegion, math:BayesFactor, and math:PosteriorProbability under math:BayesianResult (posterior semantics). Because math:FrequentistResult owl:disjointWith math:BayesianResult, the disjointness math:ConfidenceInterval ⊥ math:CredibleInterval (and math:ConfidenceRegion ⊥ math:CredibleRegion) is ENTAILED by these placements — no redundant direct owl:disjointWith is minted, and the conflation of a confidence and a credible interval is its own failure identity (math:IntervalKindConflation), the native DL coherence gate forcing a both-typed node to owl:Nothing and the paired math:IntervalKindConflationShape surfacing it as a finding. The paradigm-neutral math:PredictionInterval, math:ToleranceInterval, math:EffectSize, and math:Prediction MUST stay under math:MathematicalObject, free of either family, because they are computed in both paradigms." .

# --- Inference: the interval and effect-size hard-rule failures are typed (MUST) --- #
ex:saIntervalFailureHierarchy a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    math:IntervalKindConflation      rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:IncompleteConfidenceInterval rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:IncompleteCredibleInterval  rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
    math:UnframedEffectSize          rdfs:subClassOf math:MathConformanceFailure .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Each of the four interval and effect-size hard-rule failures MUST be a subclass of math:MathConformanceFailure, so a confidence/credible interval conflation, an incomplete confidence interval, an incomplete credible interval, and an unframed effect size are each typed, queryable objects — first-class failure classes, not log lines. math:IntervalKindConflation is the failure identity of the entailed math:ConfidenceInterval ⊥ math:CredibleInterval disjointness." .
